{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"frangible-irongray-adouri","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Symptom\n`rebar transition <id> in_progress closed` fails from the globally installed build with:\n\n```\nImportError: cannot import name 'commit_impact' from 'rebar._engine_support'\n  File \".../src/rebar/_commands/close_precheck.py\", line 283, in _check_file_impact_vs_diff\n```\n\nObserved against the pipx release snapshot `~/.local/state/rebar-dev/releases/d83fb4f6fdafeafa696238e76eff6933e5674607.98469`. The same close succeeds from the repo checkout's editable venv, so the module is present in the source tree (`src/rebar/_engine_support/commit_impact.py`, 6086 bytes, present at origin/main and in a worktree at 0b851c8103) but missing from — or unimportable in — the packaged release.\n\n## Why it matters beyond one host\n`close_precheck._check_file_impact_vs_diff` is on the completion-gate path, so this breaks closing ANY ticket that records `file_impact` when running a packaged build rather than a checkout. That is the normal path for an operator or agent using an installed rebar.\n\n## The compounding defect: it exits 0\nThe traceback is printed and the process still reports `[exited with code 0]`. A caller checking the exit status concludes the close succeeded when the ticket is untouched. That silent-success behaviour is arguably the more serious half of this bug: an automated agent will record a close that never happened. A crashing precheck must exit non-zero.\n\n## Repro\n1. Install rebar as a package (pipx from a commit at or after the one that introduced `_engine_support/commit_impact.py`).\n2. Take any ticket with a non-empty `file_impact` and the completion gate enabled.\n3. `rebar transition <id> in_progress closed` -> ImportError, exit 0, ticket unchanged.\n\n## Expected\nEither the module ships in the release (packaging/`MANIFEST`/package-data fix), or the import is resolved in a way that survives packaging; and a precheck that raises exits non-zero so the failure is not mistaken for success.\n\n## Discovery context\nHit while closing RP-02 story convergent-pinelike-lunamoth. Worked around by closing from a git worktree using the checkout's venv build. Note this host auto-updates its global rebar hourly from origin/main, so the broken snapshot is a build of main, not a stale tagged release.","id":"08c8-2236-376f-435e","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Packaged rebar release omits _engine_support/commit_impact.py, breaking every close with file_impact"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787169313728431001,"uuid":"92bde4d2-0170-4ac8-b7f1-d2788d1a4d32"}